1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,500
Auto-repair. Auto-loot. Selling junk. Your UI already does that.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,500
SMoRG's QoL does the little things nobody else does.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,100
Finish a quest objective…

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,000
…and the Human worker asks: “More work?”

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,400
Finish the whole quest…

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,000
“Job's done!” Ready to turn in.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Playing Horde? Switch to the Peon.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Above the mob: your quest count (1/7) and your range in yards.

9
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,500
Progress messages go from red through yellow to green.

10
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,700
The last quilboar…

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,000
“Work complete.” Each sound has its own on/off switch.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
New quests are tracked automatically.

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Item level and speed on your player frame.

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Colored XP and rep numbers. The rep bar shows % left and standing.

15
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Tooltips show who a unit is targeting. Here: you.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Achievements usually open on a wall of finished ones…

17
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,200
…now they open on the ones you haven't earned yet.

18
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:09,200
Ready check and queue pop timers, party levels: every tweak is its own checkbox.

19
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,800
Also inside: floating rep gains, cursor shake highlight, a hand-drawn combat font.

20
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:14,200
Free for Retail and WoW Forever. Search for “SMoRGs QoL”.
